From: Zork130 <12914881+Zork130@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6afe-dai: custom topologies and speaker
 feedback port from DT

Set up the DSP side of vendor speaker protection from the device tree:

- qcom,custom-topologies on the q6afe DAI node: topology definitions,
  registered with the DSP before the first port that uses one starts.
- qcom,topology per DAI: the topology the port starts with. q6afe now
  deregisters the previous one first, as a TX port won't take it twice.
- qcom,feedback-dai and qcom,feedback-channels on an RX DAI: a TX port
  carrying the amplifiers' V/I sense, started along with the RX port the
  way the vendor stacks use a hostless capture: feedback path set, RX
  started, then TX with the RX port's I2S format. Feedback failures are
  logged but don't stop playback.

OnePlus 8 Pro: NXP TFADSP topologies on TERTIARY_MI2S_RX/TX.

diff -ru a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodlep.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodlep.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodlep.dts	2026-11-02 16:28:29.657521054 +0000
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodlep.dts	2026-11-02 16:29:53.909024405 +0000
@@ -1204,14 +1204,28 @@
 };
 
 &q6afedai {
+	/*
+	 * NXP TFADSP speaker protection topologies, from the vendor
+	 * Global_cal.acdb: a count, then {version 2, topology, domains,
+	 * module count, {module, flags}...} records.
+	 */
+	qcom,custom-topologies = <2
+		2 0x1000b910 2 1 0x1000b911 0x10000
+		2 0x1000b909 2 1 0x1000b912 0x18000>;
+
 	dai@20 {
 		reg = <TERTIARY_MI2S_RX>;
 		qcom,sd-lines = <1>;
+		qcom,topology = <0x1000b910>;
+		/* Both amplifiers' current sense: 1, 2 top, 3, 4 bottom */
+		qcom,feedback-dai = <TERTIARY_MI2S_TX>;
+		qcom,feedback-channels = <1 2 3 4>;
 	};
 
 	dai@21 {
 		reg = <TERTIARY_MI2S_TX>;
 		qcom,sd-lines = <0>;
+		qcom,topology = <0x1000b909>;
 	};
 
 	dai@104 {
